course: dictionary
lesson: 3504
title: Old-fashioned and fashioned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have two jobs. «Old-fashioned» describes something from an earlier time that is no longer common, like an old-fashioned phone with a curly cord. «The way a character speaks, posh, rough, local or old-fashioned, helps to show what they are like.» Here old-fashioned describes the way someone speaks.
explain: Fashioned can also be the past form of the verb fashion. It means made or shaped by hand. «Ana fashioned a raft from sticks and string.» Ana did not buy the raft. She made it, so fashioned means made by hand.
explain: How do you know which meaning is right? Look at the words around it. If you see «old» or an earlier time, think old-fashioned. If you see a maker, materials like sticks or clay, or the words fashioned from or fashioned into, think made by hand.
fact: «Old-fashioned» means belonging to an earlier time and no longer common or modern.
fact: Fashioned, as a verb, means made or shaped by hand, often from simple materials.
fact: Fashion, fashions, fashioned and fashioning all come from the same root word.
fact: Useful phrases are «old-fashioned», «good old-fashioned», «fashioned from» and «fashioned into».
fact: The context tells you the meaning: «old» or an earlier time points to old-fashioned, while a maker and materials point to fashioned.
exercise: Grandad's old-fashioned phone had buttons and no screen. What does old-fashioned mean? | *From an earlier time and no longer common | Made of gold | Brand new and very modern | Loud and noisy
exercise: «The boys fashioned a spear from a long stick.» What does fashioned mean here? | Bought from a shop | *Made by hand from simple materials | Painted bright red | Lost in the long grass
exercise: «The hut was fashioned from mud and reeds.» Which clue tells you fashioned means made by hand? | *from mud and reeds | was | The hut | It is a hut
test: «The way a character speaks, posh, rough, local or old-fashioned, helps to show what they are like.» In this sentence, old-fashioned describes | Speed | A kind of food | *The way someone speaks | A place on a map
test: «The clockmaker fashioned a tiny gear out of brass.» What does fashioned mean? | Broke | *Made by hand | Bought online | Lost
exam: Jo says, «This old-fashioned game is fashioned from wood.» Which word describes the game as belonging to an earlier time? | game | *old-fashioned | fashioned | wood
